{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact R3b head b6024de490cfcc6ca6c24c6d1699302ca4b70b8d on builder/reusable-observation-r3b-20261109, tree 2c97c324, all 11 artifacts, for request 22b57b9e under promise 26d84746 and review request c3f4fd68. The reusable observation store now holds at most 4,096 records and 8 MiB of measured payload. An admitted key's handle survives an eviction from the denied FIFO. The head follows rulings 1f159465, e838bb78 and 5da28958.\n\nWhat I checked in the source:\n\n- The store. `ObservationCache.set` measures the record, then refuses it and drops any older record of the same name when the measure throws, is not a safe integer or exceeds the byte ceiling. Otherwise it replaces in place, adjusts the byte total and drops from the oldest end until both ceilings hold. `Map.set` on an existing name keeps its FIFO place. `refresh` re-measures only when the cached object is still the one sealed, so a newer replacement stays intact.\n- The measure. `observationPayloadBytes` canonicalizes the name, observation, run and read number, last-use entry and time, and every value copy, then counts UTF-8 bytes. `last.observation` is left out because it shares `observation`. The note states that this measures payload, not heap.\n- The wiring. `reusable` is the only changed structure in `further`. `one()` still inserts only non-once answers. `hand()` now copies each newly exposed record into the input's own `mine` map, so a later replacement or eviction cannot change an answer that an input already holds. `sealed` refreshes the record's weight after it records the last use.\n- The handles. `deniedRead` is undefined for an admitted key, so its `held()` and `sealed()` no longer depend on the FIFO and judge its kept record as before. A denied key's handle returns null once the FIFO no longer holds the exact record that the handle captured. `read` still compares the generation after the await, so every Membership read in flight at an eviction returns null. That keeps the R3a eviction control valid, and the five changed lines fit ruling 5da28958's limit.\n- The seals. I recomputed both outside the builder's worktree. authority.ts gives 095a2c0f… and observation-cache.ts gives d43f96c5…, each equal to its literal.\n- The threat model. It states the store's ceilings, what they measure, the first-use pin, that replay does not read the store, and the limit: no heap bound and no bound on records held by inputs at once. It also states the narrowed eviction residual in the wording ruling 5da28958 asks for.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main fade0074 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 11 paths that its 11 artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes: 7 checked, 0 flagged. No dependency, lockfile, Wrangler, definition, pin, recorded-format or migration file changes.\n- The tests. The store's Node case covers the count ceiling, the byte ceiling with fixed byte counts, the replacement order and the oversized namesake. The signed Native witness sends acts naming 4,097 absent members in batches of 64 through real signatures, Membership, the Scope and SQLite. It checks both ceilings after each batch, then shows that `@una` is read fresh inside the window with the accepted outcome. The one changed authority assertion is the one that the ruling changes: key 5000's handle stays current after the eviction.\n- The controls. Restoring unbounded insertion fails the signed witness at \"to be less than or equal to 4096\". Removing `generation++` fails the eviction case at \"to be null\". Each baseline exits 0, each fault exits 1, and both sources are restored.\n- The gate. I read gate.exit at 1fe7b6cf, tree 96c9da02: \"exit 0\". Node 145, Counting 56, Plain 4,028 plus one skip, and Native 1,133 plus two skips. The selector ran all six Scale cases because `scripts/test.mjs` changes. After the gate, only the note and the gate manifest change. Between the focused checkpoint ef12271d and the gate, only the note and the pre-gate manifest change.\n- The evidence. The two manifests hash to the cited values, 367069e2… and 2f918a78…. Their six files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One small module owns the FIFO and both ceilings. authority.ts keeps the order of reads and judgments and passes the run's measure in. Nothing becomes public.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Act content can still choose subjects, but it can no longer grow the store past 4,096 records or 8 MiB. A dropped answer costs a fresh trusted read and adds no refusal. Two limits hold by design, and the threat model states both. Records pinned by inputs that run at the same time are outside the ceilings. An eviction from the denied FIFO makes the reads in flight at that instant unanswered.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note: `hand()` walks the whole store on each call, as main did, and now also leaves each record it exposes pinned in the input's `mine` map. That is up to 4,096 references per input, and the threat model already counts them outside the ceilings.\n\nThe planner deploys after landing. No setting changes. This approval authorizes no deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:75ba0a010f492b516e6512c08b3853d7afc59c00","binding":"assigned","head":"b6024de490cfcc6ca6c24c6d1699302ca4b70b8d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1e4e8fd35f780b5118e5cce7fd7a51e1fc0e063f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:26d847463c52af40d0acf925cfb2c90da4461cd9\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1e4e8fd35f780b5118e5cce7fd7a51e1fc0e063f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}